// The Clang module `SafariServices` for Objective-C code (route b), shaped
// like the SDK's SafariServices.framework module: `@import SafariServices;`
// brings in Foundation, UIKit (OpenUIKit's Objective-C interfaces) and
// SFSafariViewController, and re-exports them (`export *`).
//
// Why a separate module map: SwiftPM's generated map for the Swift
// SafariServices target has no `export *`, so an importer saw neither
// Foundation's macros nor NSException (MEASURED, NetNewsWire's
// SFSafariViewController+Extras.h: "unknown type name
// 'NS_ASSUME_NONNULL_BEGIN'"), and two maps defining one module name are a
// redefinition. Objective-C targets therefore depend on the product
// `SafariServicesObjC`; Swift targets keep the Swift `SafariServices`
// (docs/agent_reports/safari-objc.md).
module SafariServices {
  header "SafariServicesObjC.h"
  export *
}
